    {
      "id": "sol.amc-8-1998-p12.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "For each integer \\(n\\) from \\(2\\) through \\(10,\\)\n\n\\[n\\left(1-\\frac{1}{n}\\right)=n-1.\\]\n\nThe expression is therefore \\(1+2+\\cdots+9=45.\\)\n\nThus, the correct answer is A .",
      "hints": [
        "Simplify each term \\(n(1-\\frac{1}{n}).\\)",
        "The terms become consecutive integers."
